  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It passes the typecheck, but I couldn't run it, so I haven't seen it render. It draws 64 boxes in a ring of radius 5 as one `instances.box` node, with a shadow-receiving floor plane under the `product-studio` look. That look supplies the lighting and shadows, with exposure lowered by 0.8 EV. Each frame the bar heights come from a sum of four sine waves, and `setInstances` is called with the transforms and colours. Colours are a hue gradient around the ring, converted to hex because the engine doesn't parse `hsl()` strings. The camera orbits slowly through `app.camera?.setPose`. I found no documentation showing that `setPose` works with the `camera.perspective` camera I declared, so the orbit is the part most likely not to move. Bars are rotated about Y to face outward, assuming radians. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame and again after `app.ready()`.",
